throughout the day on saturday small  groups of people arrived to pay their  respects on clapham common  near the bandstand close to the spot  where sarah everard was last seen  so how did this quiet dignified  spectacle  descend into this  we've analyzed video footage from that  afternoon and evening  giving insight into some of the key  moments  by four o'clock we see the first signs  that numbers are swelling here  with around 200 people gathered near the  bandstand  around half past five and a steady  stream of people  are now heading here it's clear that  although the original vigil was  cancelled  many are determined to be here it is a  conflict  between all of us and the state  15 minutes later it's obvious not  everyone here  is solely focused on just having a vigil  [Applause]  but although there were people here from  different groups some with different  agendas  the bulk of the crowd were clearly here  to take part in a vigil for sarah  by six o'clock the crowd had grown to  more than 500  in response the police presence is also  slowly increasing  as a minute silence is held in memory of  sarah everard  at this point a key moment as a local  councillor can be heard urging people to  begin leaving  so thank you for coming this evening we  do all need to disperse  obviously peacefully and everything else  but thank you all very much for joining  us  in an aerial image we've highlighted  small pockets of police officers  mainly on the edges of the crowd  scotland yards say  it's at this point they were trying to  persuade people to leave  almost half an hour later with no  discernible change in the crowd size  a police liaison officer makes a direct  appeal to people to leave  nobody here is socially distanced  and we're asking people to go home  [Applause]  few here appear to be listening from 6  30  another potentially pivotal moment as  police commanders decide to move more  officers  up onto the bandstand the atmosphere has  shifted  things are much more this is no longer a  ritual  too many people in one place  that's dangerous within 20 minutes  the bandstand is almost surrounded by  officers  20 minutes after that addressing the  crowd  patsy stevenson now an iconic figure  after the pictures of her subsequent  arrest were flashed around the world  here she's urging the crowd to resist  the calls to disperse  the police  [Applause]  just after twenty past seven another key  moment in our sequence of events  as police take the decision to start  removing people from the front of the  bandstand  including patsy stevenson  [Applause]  it's at this point that the tensions  here spill over  into scuffles and arrests the image of  patsy stevenson  penned to the ground by male officers  united all sides of the political  spectrum  and beyond in a shared sense of alarm  by 8 pm the crowd around the band stand  is beginning to disperse  but an angry group can be seen following  officers  as they take those arrested back to  their vans  it is far from the dignified evening of  reflection  the original organizers had planned  the video timeline of events captures  the key moments of escalation  that led to the scenes of disorder but  it'll be up to the independent inquiry  to determine whether that crucial police  decision  to move in and disperse people was the  correct course of action  mark white sky news
 

